  "description": "`about` is the item the phone has open when its owner speaks (ADR 0214), on a `POST /inherent/submit` from a paired device (and on a `say`, whose own refusal is `error bad_say`). It is an object of `kind` (one of `kinds`) and `id` (1 to `limits.id_chars` characters of letters, digits and `_-=+/.|:@`; a longer one is refused, never cut), with an optional `title` (text; the brain flattens it to one line and clips it to `limits.title_chars`) and `start_ms` (an integer epoch ms between 0 and `limits.start_ms`). A stretch of what he was doing (`kind` `doing`, ADR 0410) is named by its time: it needs `start_ms` and an `end_ms` after it, up to the same limit, and the brain finds it by that window, not by its id, which changes when the lane is cut again; no other kind may carry `end_ms`. No other key is allowed. A valid case that the brain changes names what it becomes in `becomes`. An invalid `about` is a 422; an `about` from the local key rather than a paired device is a 400.",
